THE GOTCHA THIS SLICE EXISTS FOR — ledger.mjs's own seq allocator is single-process. Pattern (ledger.mjs:624-643):
  function nextSeq(adwId, kind) {
    const key = `${adwId}:${kind}`
    if (!seqAllocators.has(key)) {
      let max = 0
      const conn = ensureDb()
      if (conn) { /* SELECT MAX(seq) ... */ }
      seqAllocators.set(key, max)
    }
    const next = seqAllocators.get(key) + 1
    seqAllocators.set(key, next); return next
  }
It seeds from SELECT MAX(seq) ONCE per process per (adw_id, kind). BELOW THE NODE FLOOR ensureDb() returns null so max is ALWAYS 0 — every below-floor process restarts numbering at 1, a deterministic 100% collision, not a race. UNIQUE(adw_id, seq) + INSERT OR IGNORE then silently drops the loser, and replayJsonl re-drops it. #41 is the first multi-process caller, so every emission from this facade must pass an EXPLICIT seq drawn from a parent-allocated, sidecar-persisted range — never rely on nextSeq.

MIRROR-FAILURE SEMANTICS ALREADY IN LEDGER.MJS (ledger.mjs:604-622): appendJsonl may THROW (that is deliberate — losing the raw record is fatal to the caller); the sqlite mirror() is already try/catch'd and only bumps stats.mirror_errors. Your facade's catch therefore exists for the JSONL throw, an open failure, and your own lock/resolver failures — which is exactly why #41 needs its OWN counters and its own reader: ledger.stats() reports {degraded, mirror_errors, mirror_first_code, dropped_payload_keys, redacted_values, degraded_reason} for the HANDLE's failures only (ledger.mjs:1164-1166, :502-512).

LOCK/EXCLUSIVE-CREATE PATTERN TO MIRROR — dispatch.mjs's await lock (scripts/cmux/dispatch.mjs:1801-1820):
  function tryAcquireAwaitLock(lockPath, holder, capS) {
    for (let attempt = 0; attempt < 2; attempt += 1) {
      try { writeFileSync(lockPath, JSON.stringify(holder), { flag: 'wx' }); return { acquired: true } }
      catch (e) {
        if (e.code !== 'EEXIST') throw e
        const existing = readJsonOrWarn(lockPath, 'await.lock')
        const startedMs = existing ? Date.parse(existing.started_at) : NaN
        const isStale = !existing || !Number.isFinite(startedMs) || Date.now() - startedMs > capS * 2 * 1000
        if (attempt === 0 && isStale) { unlinkIfExists(lockPath); continue }
        return { acquired: false, holder: existing }
      }
    }
  }
Release only if the on-disk lock still carries THIS holder's exact pid + started_at (dispatch.mjs:2017-2025) — a late-waking superseded holder must never delete a successor's lock. Your version differs in one way: retry a fixed budget (20 x 50ms) rather than twice, then give up and count.

